# Copy to .env.local for local development. Both values are public by D14 — the
# anon key ships inside a static bundle any visitor can read, so it is a routing
# key rather than an authorisation key, and RLS is the only access control.
#
# In CI these are repository **variables**, not secrets (§14.2). Marking them
# secret would only hide from the next maintainer that they are public.
#
# The service-role key is NOT here and never will be (S2). It lives in an
# untracked .env.local used by /casio-catalog requests, and in a password
# manager. Nothing in CI needs it, including D23's keep-alive ping.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# D68 — the GA4 measurement ID. Public by the same argument as the anon key: it
# ships in the bundle and identifies a property rather than authorising anything.
#
# LEAVE IT UNSET LOCALLY. It is what switches analytics on, so an ID here posts
# your own browsing into the production property, and it is also what widens the
# Content-Security-Policy for Google's hosts — the grant and the script arrive
# together or neither does. In CI it is a repository **variable** (§14.2),
# alongside the two above.
VITE_GA_ID=
